:: day_4_1b

I didn't want to check. The way you don't want to look at a wound, not because you can't handle the sight of blood but because looking makes it real, gives it permission to exist, transforms it from a sensation you can ignore into a fact you have to confront.

I looked. I pushed my smallclothes down past my hips   the hips that were wider than yesterday, the hipbones that jutted at an angle my hands didn't recognize   and looked down at myself.

My cock was the same. That was the first thing I checked and the first relief I felt, a wash of cold gratitude that hit my chest and made my breath shudder. Same length, same girth, the familiar weight of it hanging between my thighs, the foreskin loose in its resting state, the shaft and head unchanged. I cupped myself   the gesture automatic, the way every man touches himself when checking that everything's still where it should be   and the feel of it was the same. Heavy. Warm. Present.

But the territory around it was shifting. The coarse dark pubic hair was thinner. Not gone   still there, still recognizably mine   but finer, the individual strands less wiry, the overall density reduced. The skin of my inner thighs was softer, the rough texture smoothing out the same way my face and chest had smoothed, and when my fingers brushed the crease of my groin   the fold where thigh met pelvis   the sensitivity was startling. A zing of sensation, almost ticklish, almost erotic, that ran from the crease up into my lower belly and made my breath catch.

My thighs themselves were   I turned to the side in the mirror. Still muscular. Still the thick, powerful legs of a man who walked for a living and fought on his feet. But the shape was different. Marginally. The muscle sat differently on the bone, the quadriceps less bulging, the outer line smoother and there was   I pressed my hand against the outer thigh   softness. A thin layer of something between the skin and the muscle that hadn't been there before. Not fat, exactly. Cushioning. Padding. The earliest deposit of a redistribution that my body was executing without my consent.

My balls. I cupped them again, deliberately this time, feeling for changes. They were   the same. I thought. The scrotum was maybe smoother, the skin there following the same softening trend as everywhere else, but the testicles inside felt unchanged. Present. Accounted for. Still doing whatever testicles did when they weren't actively trying to ruin your life.

I pulled my smallclothes back up. My hands were shaking. Not badly   a fine tremor, the vibration of adrenaline and fear running through muscle that wasn't sure whether to fight or run and couldn't do either because the enemy was inside the walls.

I looked at my forearms. The hair there had been "thinner" yesterday. Today it was   retreating. Visibly, noticeably retreating. The dark forest of arm hair that I'd had since adolescence had been replaced by fine, sparse growth that lay flat against skin that gleamed with new smoothness. I could see the veins more clearly now, the blue-green tracery of blood vessels visible through skin that had lost its roughness and its camouflage simultaneously.

My hands. I turned them over. The calluses   the thick ridges of keratin that ten years of swordwork had deposited on my palms, the hard currency of my profession, the evidence that my hands knew how to do one thing well   were thinning. Visibly. The edges softer, the ridges lower, the rough protective layer that stood between my skin and the world being sanded down by whatever alchemical engine was running inside me. I pressed my palm against the rough wood of the windowsill and the texture screamed at me   vivid, amplified, every splinter and grain rendered in high definition by nerve endings that had been turned up to frequencies I'd never registered before.

The scar through my left eyebrow. I touched it. Still there. The thin diagonal line from a knife fight at twenty-one, raised and pale and exactly where it had always been. The one constant. The anchor in a body that was setting sail without consulting its captain.

I leaned close to the mirror. Looked into my own eyes. Green. Deep-set. Hooded lids. The same eyes that had stared back at me from every reflection since I was old enough to care about reflections. The same eyes. Still mine. Everything else   increasingly negotiable.

