:: day_4_3a
<<set $day_4_3a = true>>
I tried the handle. Unlocked. The door swung inward on quiet hinges, revealing Nothing. The room was the same   stone walls, low ceiling, the sound of water running somewhere beneath the floor. The shelves were there. The heavy wooden table. The oil lamps, cold and dark. The smell of herbs and clean chemicals.
/* <img src="img/scene/day_4/6.png" style="width: 100%; max-width: 768px; margin: 0 auto;" /> */
But it was half-empty. Bottles missing from the shelves, gaps in the neat rows like missing teeth. The surgical instruments   the forceps, the needles, the small bone saw   gone. The white cloth from the smaller table   gone. The leather apron on the hook by the door   gone.

She'd packed. Deliberately, selectively. Not a hasty departure   a planned one. The remaining bottles on the shelves were organized, the labels facing outward, as if arranged for someone who'd need to find things after she left. A pot of the wound salve sat on the table with a strip of cloth wrapped around it, a deliberate leaving-behind and beside the salve, a note.

<<dialog "Mira">>
Don't touch it.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Aldric">>
It's a piece of parchment, not a trap.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Mira">>
In a witch's abandoned laboratory, everything is potentially a trap. Including parchment.
<</dialog>>

I picked up the note. It did not explode, dissolve, or transform me into anything more than I was already being transformed into. Small victories.

The handwriting was precise, measured, each letter formed with the care of a woman who treated communication as a craft:

The process has begun and will continue regardless of intervention. It is not poison. It is not disease. It is change, and change completes itself on its own schedule.

My apprentice will remain for those who need ongoing care. Her name is Nella. She will be here by mid-morning.

I am sorry that I cannot be here to guide this in person. Circumstances require my departure. What I can tell you: the compound requires thirty days to complete its cycle. On the thirty-first day, the process will have stabilized entirely.

There is a way to reverse the effects. At any stage. I possess the counter-formula. When you are ready   if you are ready   come find me.

The road northeast. Thornfield Priory, five days. Blackthorn Market, seven days. I will be at one or the other.

Y.

I read it twice. Three times. Each time, the words rearranged themselves into a different kind of horror.

