Tomorrow. The road. The escort. The search.

The water stain on the ceiling was invisible in the dark. But I knew it was there. The horse shape. The cracks in the plaster. The same ceiling I'd stared at for a week, unchanged while everything beneath it changed. Tomorrow I'd wake up under a different ceiling   a sky ceiling, an open-road ceiling, the vast indifferent sky that didn't give a damn about one man's body or one witch's formula or the twenty-seven days of transformation that stretched ahead like a road I hadn't chosen to walk.

But I was walking it. One day at a time. One change at a time. One morning mirror at a time and Mira was walking it with me. Behind me, holding on, her arm across my waist, her breath on my neck, her knee tucked behind mine in the familiar geometry of two people who'd found a way to fit together and were now discovering what happened when one of them was reshaped by forces beyond either of their control.

Under my skin, in the dark, the compound worked. Patient. Relentless. Uninterested in my opinion on the matter.

The body knows what it needs.

I didn't agree. But the body wasn't asking.

I slept. Badly. But I slept.

[[Wake Up|end_of_cuurent_version]]